-- CK-142: a derived-row template too deep to publish is reported, not
-- published as a silent `<error>`. `A.eq` needs `a.foo` at a method type
-- 509 tuples deep, which A's own writer and every reader accept. `B.W`'s
-- derived `eq` row wraps that requirement in two more levels, past the
-- writer's 512. At 8b98464 `Facts.templateScheme` calls `writer.add` outside
-- the one publication routine: no `hasError` scan, and on `too_deep` it
-- publishes `<error>` with no `noteDeepDecl`. So `check A B` exits 0, and C
-- — a valid use — gets two INTERNAL ERRORs at `C.beni:15:23` (the Debug
-- binary panics on I7). Expected: B's row goes through `Publisher.scheme`
-- and B reports NESTING TOO DEEP (the position is open: §14.1 does not yet
-- say which region a row's failure names), and C, reading a poisoned row,
-- says nothing. Oracle twin: at 508 tuples the program checks.
pub type Box a
    = Box a


